---
import SubpageLayout from '@layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';

const _body = `
<section class="post-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="post-hero-meta">
      <a href="/blog.html" class="section-label" style="text-decoration:none">← Blog</a>
      <span class="post-date">September 16, 2026</span>
      <span class="badge">Release</span>
      <span class="badge">Runtime</span>
      <span class="badge">Models</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="t-h1">Traverse v0.12.0: exact-ref model.execute</h1>
    <div class="post-byline">
      <span>By <strong>Enrico Piovesan</strong></span>
      <span>3 min read</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="container">
  <div class="post-layout">

    <article class="post-prose">

      <p><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.12.0">Traverse v0.12.0</a> ships Spec <code>138-governed-exact-model-execution</code> / ADR-0074: host-staged <code>model.execute</code> for WASM model packages an app has pinned by digest — never by a naked URL.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        Short version: declare <code>exact_model_dependencies</code>, stage tensors through opaque refs, call Spec 137 <code>model.execute</code>, and get fail-closed pin / digest / policy checks on native and browser <code>wasm-cpu</code>. Same envelopes. No provider authority fields on the payload.
      </div>

      <h2 id="why">Why a minor</h2>

      <p>This is new public capability on the existing Spec 137 host-connector port, not a patch. Connector contract <code>traverse.model-runtime</code> moves to <strong>2.0.0</strong>. crates.io and npm are lockstep at <code>0.12.0</code>. Pin <code>traverse-registry =0.22.0</code> if you consume the registry crate directly. The certified <code>runtime.wasm</code> digest is unchanged from 0.11.0.</p>

      <h2 id="what">What shipped</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Host-owned package store with single-consume staged I/O refs and fail-closed policy / pin / digest checks.</li>
        <li>CPU-WASM guest ABI (<code>model_execute</code> + LE feature frames) and the echo fixture under <code>fixtures/models/fixture-echo-1.0.0/</code>.</li>
        <li><code>traverse-embedder-web</code> stage / execute / read helpers matching native <code>ExactModelHostConnector</code>.</li>
        <li>Specs 044 / 045 / 137 amended for exact pins and authority-free payloads.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="upgrade">Upgrade note</h2>

      <p>Apps that want local exact-ref models must declare <code>exact_model_dependencies</code> (Spec 044) and use <code>model_ref</code> digests that match those pins. Provider authority fields on <code>model.execute</code> payloads fail closed. Pin <code>traverse-embedder-web@0.12.0</code> together with crates at <code>0.12.0</code>.</p>

      <h2 id="bounds">Honest bounds</h2>

      <p>First conformance is <code>wasm-cpu</code>. Spec 045 (candidate / LLM resolution) stays a separate track. Guest <code>model_invoke</code> remains out of scope for Spec 138 v1. This cut does not claim that every host already ships a certified public model-runtime package beyond the published path.</p>

      <p>Longer explainer: <a href="/questions/what-is-exact-ref-model-execution.html">What is exact-ref model execution?</a></p>

      <p>Full notes: <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.12.0">GitHub Release</a> · <a href="/changelog.html">site changelog</a>.</p>

    </article>

    <aside class="post-sidebar">
      <div class="sidebar-card">
        <div class="sidebar-title">In this post</div>
        <ul class="toc-list">
          <li><a href="#why">Why a minor</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what">What shipped</a></li>
          <li><a href="#upgrade">Upgrade note</a></li>
          <li><a href="#bounds">Honest bounds</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-cta">
        <div class="sidebar-title">Get the cut</div>
        <p><code>cargo add traverse-runtime@0.12.0</code><br/><code>npm i traverse-embedder-web@0.12.0</code></p>
        <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.12.0" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Release →</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>
</div>
`;
---
<SubpageLayout
  title="Traverse v0.12.0: exact-ref model.execute"
  description="Spec 138 / ADR-0074: host-staged model.execute for digest-pinned WASM model packages on native and browser wasm-cpu. crates.io and npm at 0.12.0."
  canonical="https://traverse-framework.com/blog/traverse-0-12-0-exact-ref-model-execute.html"
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Blog', href: '/blog.html' }]}
>
  <style is:global slot="head">.post-hero-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .post-date { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .post-hero h1 { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .post-byline { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--fg-muted); flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .post-byline strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; }
    .post-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 280px; gap: 4rem; padding: 3.5rem 0 5rem; align-items: start; }
    @media (max-width: 900px) { .post-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; } .post-sidebar { order: -1; } }
    .post-prose { max-width: 680px; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--fg); }
    .post-prose p { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
    .post-prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; color: var(--fg); }
    .post-prose ol, .post-prose ul { margin: 0 0 1.4rem 1.25rem; }
    .post-prose li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .post-prose a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--accent-dim); }
    .post-prose a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }
    .post-prose code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85em; background: var(--bg-elevated); padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; color: var(--accent); }
    .callout { background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.75rem 0; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .post-sidebar { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 2rem); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .sidebar-card { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; }
    .sidebar-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
    .toc-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
    .toc-list a { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--fg-muted); text-decoration: none; display: block; padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem; border-left: 2px solid transparent; transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s; }
    .toc-list a:hover { color: var(--fg); border-left-color: var(--accent); }
    .sidebar-cta { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--bg-elevated), var(--bg-card)); border-color: var(--accent-dim); }
    .sidebar-cta p { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--fg-muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }</style>
  <Fragment set:html={_body} />
</SubpageLayout>
